  "causalChain": [
    "A presenter types notes while moving between slides or changing canvas zoom. Controls cover typed text and can cover one another.",
    "SlideCanvas renders viewport, pager, conditional notes and zoom as sibling children of the same canvas panel; the notes are an in-flow implicit grid row.",
    "nodeslide.css:926 establishes a positioned, clipped grid panel; nodeslide.css:1252 takes pager/zoom out of flow with position:absolute. Their containing block includes the notes.",
    "nodeslideV3.css:1866 allocates only the viewport row explicitly; nodeslideV3.css:1926/1931 anchors both groups at bottom:0 rather than allocating separate space.",
    "Zoom inherits left:50% and translateX(-50%) from nodeslide.css:1265 while V3 also sets right:12px. Phone V3:5201 re-enables the pager. No shared flow layout prevents the two intrinsic groups from colliding."
  ],
  "recommendedOwners": [
    "src/domains/nodeslide/components/SlideCanvas.tsx",
    "src/domains/nodeslide/nodeslide.css",
    "src/domains/nodeslide/nodeslideV3.css"
  ],
  "recommendation": "Put the existing pager and zoom groups in one plain in-flow control-row wrapper directly after the canvas viewport; place the conditional notes strip after that row. Give the panel explicit viewport/control/notes rows (and existing metadata row where visible). Use a wrapping flex row, normal-flow groups and a single owned reset of position/insets/transform. Preserve all current handlers and note lifecycle.",
  "implementationConstraints": [
    "No measured note-height React state, guessed bottom offsets, z-index workaround, dependency, public API or timer.",
    "Remove or replace competing owned positioning rules instead of stacking another late override.",
    "Use content-driven row/group height and preserve readable Fit/value/count labels at text200; wrapping may produce two rows.",
    "Keep visible previous/next boundary disabling, current slide identity/count, 40..120 zoom range and Fit=65 behavior.",
    "Keep slide.id notes remount, version-keyed textarea, exact Unicode/line breaks and existing save-on-blur.",
    "Keep hidden pan control hidden in this skin; test existing Space/pan only where applicable. Do not count its zero box as a visible failed control.",
    "Do not expand into navigation, graph density, backend/notes durability policy, provider, export or native Office."
  ],
  "proofPlan": [
    "Preserve the ten current before cells and three labelled boundary PNGs. Correct only future stage measurement selector from .ns-slide-stage to actual .ns-canvas-stage; prior missing measurement stays recorded.",
    "Repeat same six normal widths 320/390/768/1024/1440/1920, text200 at390/1440 and collapsed390/1440. Capture DOM, console and pixels per cell before resizing.",
    "Require non-overlapping notes/control group rectangles and actual rendered enabled-control hit targets. Check full label ink bounds; a textarea center hit alone cannot prove its last lines are uncovered.",
    "Use native keyboard and pointer: enter exact multiline Unicode notes, blur via Next, return Previous and reload to verify same slide ID/current notes; repeat first/last disabled boundaries and collapsed/open toggles.",
    "Burst sequence zoom out/in/Fit then slide back/forward and notes toggle; sustained one-minute repeated navigation/notes editing confirms identities, current values, no duplicate save or stale note overwrite.",
    "Exercise viewport scroll, vertical textarea resize, no-notes/read-only state and one landscape-height cell if the layout otherwise risks consuming all canvas height. Preserve canvas/inspector neighbors outside the declared expected row-height shift.",
    "Run relevant existing component/navigation/notes scenarios and normal required check once after exact source freeze. Retain any inherited timing failures; do not raise deadlines or add skips.",
    "Independent bounded after replay should cover representative390 text200 and1440 normal plus the original320 blocked-Next case. No whole-grade claim."
